OpenXTOS licensing notice
=========================

OpenXTOS combines components under different licenses. This file explains
which parts are covered by which license and how they relate.

1. Apache-2.0 (repository LICENSE)
----------------------------------
Applies to the XTOS-authored user-space material:
  - sdk/libxtos-rt, sdk/libxtos-signal, sdk/libxtos-bci (source and headers)
  - tools/xtos-eeg-pipeline, tools/xtos-signal-benchmark, tools/xtos-eeg-replay
  - examples/
  - system/ (rootfs skeleton, init scripts, busybox defconfig)
  - scripts/ (build and verification automation)
  - kernel/xtos_defconfig (kernel configuration fragment)

2. GPL-2.0 (kernel side)
------------------------
  - kernel/linux/ is the upstream Linux 6.6.0 source, licensed under
    GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note (see kernel/linux/COPYING).
  - kernel/patches/preempt-rt-6.6-rt15.patch is the upstream PREEMPT_RT
    patch for Linux 6.6.0-rt15 (GPL-2.0).
  - kernel/patches/xtos-linux-6.6.patch adds XTOS kernel components
    (scheduler helper, BCI core/buffer, OpenBCI Cyton driver, UAPI
    headers). These files carry "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0" and
    are kernel-space derivative work, so they are GPL-2.0.

3. GPL-2.0 (userland)
---------------------
  - userspace/busybox/ is the unmodified BusyBox 1.37.0 release source
    (GPL-2.0; see userspace/busybox/LICENSE).

4. Vendored third-party crypto sources (new in 1.0.1)
-----------------------------------------------------
  - tools/xtos-native/vendor/mbedtls: upstream Mbed TLS source under
    Apache-2.0 (see tools/xtos-native/vendor/mbedtls/LICENSE). Used only to
    build the project's native tools; not linked by the Apache-2.0 SDK.
  - tools/xtos-native/vendor/monocypher: upstream Monocypher + optional
    Ed25519, dual-licensed BSD-2-Clause / CC0-1.0 at the user's choice
    (see tools/xtos-native/vendor/monocypher/LICENCE.md).

5. AI runtime binary closure (not distributed in this tree)
-----------------------------------------------------------
  - tools/xtos-ai-runtime is project source (Apache-2.0). The private
    inference runtime binaries (CPython, ONNX Runtime and the 9-package
    lock closure) are NOT part of this source repository; they are
    assembled at build time by scripts/assemble_ai_runtime.py and
    scripts/provision_ai_runtime.py from the version- and hash-pinned
    inputs recorded in system/packages/ai-runtime-x86_64.json, under
    their upstream licenses (Python: PSF; onnxruntime: MIT).

Why the combination works
--------------------------
The Apache-2.0 user-space SDK does not link against the GPL-2.0 kernel
components. They communicate through the kernel UAPI boundary (ioctl
and syscall ABI), which is expressly not a derivative-work relationship
(the "Linux-syscall-note" in the kernel COPYING). Consequently the SDK
stays Apache-2.0 while kernel-side XTOS code is GPL-2.0.

If you modify files inside kernel/linux/, kernel/patches/, or
userspace/busybox/, your modifications of those files are governed by
their respective GPL-2.0 licenses.
